# name	repository			pipeline
# Tab separated. Copy to ~/.factory/dark-factory/projects.tsv and edit it. The
# map is per machine, not per checkout, because this skill is installed by copy
# and anything inside it is overwritten on the next install.
# "repository" must be exactly owner/name form prefixed with github.com, three
# slash separated parts. A URL form has five parts and is rejected with
# 400 invalid_repository.
# "pipeline" is optional and names one from GET /api/v1/pipelines. Empty means
# the server's default single stage pipeline. Reviewed work should select a
# pipeline ending in Factory delivery; project-specific pipelines can put one
# canonical suite in a model-free code stage.
# Delivery is deliberately absent. It is a per project setting held by the
# server and set in the cockpit, and a submission must not override it.
scratch	github.com/your-org/factory-scratch	Implement, review, deliver
